# The agent surface's own build_webui() bundle (BUILD.gn, redrob.html, redrob.css, redrob.ts) is gone
# with the C++ WebUI (A-7). What stays in redrob/ is the design system, shared by the onboarding and
# settings bundles -- design_icons.ts included: that bundle compiled it, but the integrity gate reads it
# as the vendored glyph table, so it outlives the bundle.
# One source file copied into all three WebUI bundles. build_webui's static_files are per-target and
# relative to the target's own directory, so a bundle cannot reference a file in another bundle's folder
# -- which is why the font is already duplicated three ways. Mapping one source to three destinations
# here means the duplication is in the copy step rather than on disk, so each of these has exactly one
# place it can be edited.
#
# design_tokens.css and fonts/ are the design system itself, vendored by scripts/vendor_design_system.py
# and pinned by DESIGN_SYSTEM_PIN.json. brand/ is the logo artwork, pinned in the same file by sha256 but
# from the design system DELIVERY rather than from npm, because @redrob-labs/ui ships no logo file. All of
# it is copied ONCE, into redrob/: all three bundles reach them
# through each BUILD.gn's generate_grd, whose input_files_base_dir points at that directory. The other
# shared files below are per-bundle copies because build_webui static_files cannot cross directories. chrome_base.css carries only what a
# Chromium WebUI needs and the design system deliberately does not provide, and defines no token at all.
# theme.ts gives the vendored sheet the data-theme attribute it switches on.
sources/chrome/browser/resources/redrob/design_tokens.css  chrome/browser/resources/redrob/design_tokens.css
# The component layer. ONE copy, like the fonts: all three bundles read it out of redrob/ through
# generate_grd's input_files_base_dir, so there is no per-bundle row here. It must be LINKED after
# design_tokens.css -- it supersedes two of its roles. Gate check 7.
sources/chrome/browser/resources/redrob/design_system.css  chrome/browser/resources/redrob/design_system.css

# The design system's glyph geometry (design_icons.ts) was DERIVED from its React icon module and was
